// laniusc defect: a user function named `print` is silently replaced by the
// built-in print_i32 runtime routine. No redefinition diagnostic is given.
//
// Build: laniusc --stdlib-root stdlib user_fn_print_replaced_by_builtin.lani -o out
// Expected: no output, exit status 7 (the user function's result), or a
//           compile-time error rejecting the name.
// Actual (lang, laniusc built 2026-10-28, native x86_64): prints "239089668"
//           and a newline, which is the low 32 bits of the u64 argument
//           printed as i32, and exits with 10, the byte count the built-in
//           returns. The user body never runs.
//
// Symptom seen in practice: a u64 decimal printer named `print` showed
// values above 2^31 truncated or negative. Renaming the function avoids it.
// Methods named print (impl blocks) are not affected.
module app::main;
fn print(value:u64) -> i32 { return 7; }
fn main() -> i32 {
    let big:u64=4534056964;
    return print(big);
}
